# Underwater: suspended silt plus rising bubbles in a camera-following box that lives BELOW the live
# ocean surface (Underwater true: a particle above the surface is put back at a random depth under it -
# a bubble reaching the surface pops and re-forms below; the draw hides the whole volume while the
# camera is above sea level). Tune live with Particles/Underwater count / size / alpha.
ParticleEffect Underwater
	# Silt: slow drift, a hint of settling.
	Emitter Silt
		Volume 15, 10, 15
		Count 8000
		FollowCamera true
		Underwater true
		Direction 0, 1, 0
		ConeAngle 180
		Speed 0.02 0.06
		Gravity 0.05
		Drag 2
		Turbulence 0.4 0.4 0.1
		Size 0.02 0.02
		SizeVariance 0.6
		ColorStart 0.85, 0.9, 0.85, 0.45
		ColorEnd 0.85, 0.9, 0.85, 0.45
		SoftFade 0.3
		Lit true
		EmissiveFloor 0.15
	# Bubbles: buoyant (negative gravity) against drag = a 0.33 m/s rise, with a wobble.
	Emitter Bubbles
		Volume 15, 10, 15
		Count 900
		FollowCamera true
		Underwater true
		Direction 0, 1, 0
		ConeAngle 30
		Speed 0.2 0.4
		Gravity -0.5
		Drag 1.5
		Turbulence 0.8 1.5 0.5
		Size 0.025 0.025
		SizeVariance 0.7
		ColorStart 0.9, 0.97, 1.0, 0.8
		ColorEnd 0.9, 0.97, 1.0, 0.8
		Additivity 0.5
		SoftFade 0.15
		Lit true
		EmissiveFloor 0.3
